   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Cloth Reveal\n\nA satin sheet draped over your content is yanked from one corner, folding and fluttering as a simulated cloth before it clears the frame. The Verlet simulation runs once at load with a fixed timestep and a seeded rest shape (a 32×20 grid), every frame's points are stored, and the timeline only draws the stored frame. The content under the sheet is a neutral lockup with editable text.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 2.133 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A logo, product or headline should be unveiled like a launch-event reveal.\n- The video opens on a covered shape so the viewer waits a beat for what is underneath.\n- A single premium reveal is the payoff of the video and can afford a heavier render.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The reveal is a move from one scene to the next rather than content under a sheet: use page-turn.\n- A light should search the dark stage and land on the logo: use spotlight.\n- Lines of text only need to rise into place: use mask-reveal-up.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Unveiled\"\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"right\"\n- cloth_color (color): Cloth, default \"#E5322D\"\n- underside_color (color): Underside, default \"#8E1A16\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- delay (number, 0-30): Delay, default 6\n- seed (number, 1-24): Seed, default 2\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
